# Rules of the code: {{product.name}}

This is the one file you edit to make the crew fit your product. `init.mjs` writes it once and
never overwrites it. Everything the crew does in the repository (`{{product.repo}}`) follows it.
Replace the examples below with your own facts; delete lines that do not apply.

## Run it

- Start the dev copy: `<command>` (it must answer at {{product.appUrl}})
- Dev log: `<command> > {{crew_dir}}/dev.log 2>&1` (the log watcher reads it, optional)
- Lint (run on your own files before you report): `<for example: npx eslint <files>>`
- Typecheck / tests (Boss runs them before publishing): `<for example: npm run typecheck && npm test>`
- **No test may fail.** Every worker and reviewer runs the test command above before handing work on, and the output with its pass and fail counts goes in the task update. A test that needs something that is not there (a server, a browser, a variable) skips and says why. Nobody skips, deletes or loosens a test that fails for another reason. Not knowing why it fails goes to Pia (tag `test failing`), and from Pia to Boss.

