## Release (Boss only)

0. Before merging ANY branch: merge the main branch into it (or squash it onto a fresh main in a worktree on disk,
   never in `/tmp`) and rerun everything on the result, as one command: `<for example: crew publish ...>`. Install,
   migrate on a scratch database only, typecheck, lint, the full tests. Stop on a conflict or a failure. This is the
   merger's job (Boss), not the workers': things go stale in unexpected ways fast.
1. Back up the database: `<command>`
2. Apply the schema change: `<command>`
3. Typecheck and lint (already part of step 0 on the merged tree): `<command>`
4. Merge the task's pull request (workers push their own branch; only Boss merges), with `<attribution lines, if any>`: `<command>`
5. Move the published tasks to Done.
